    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 30th is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers our highest daily efficiency at 83.29. Facing a favorable matchup against Fedde (xERA 5.20) with a dynamic platoon edge, **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear anchor of the lineup today. We are also high on **Kyle Tucker** (76.77) and **Andy Pages** (73.34); both benefit significantly from a park factor boost and a matchup against Springs, despite the L/L disadvantage. **Miguel Vargas** also presents a strong play (66.32) as he capitalizes on a weak opposing starter in Gibson, and **Cole Carrigg** (65.25) remains an intriguing utility option, with wind-aided projections and a favorable park environment pushing his score well above the baseline.\n\nThe decision to start **Nasim Nunez** (47.71) over **Nolan Schanuel** (45.47) was the tightest call on the bench. While **Nolan Schanuel** was the more efficient pure hitter, the mandate to prioritize stolen base potential keeps **Nasim Nunez** in the starting nine; his ability to exploit Early\u2019s slow delivery (88% SB success rate) provides category-specific value that outweighs the marginal gap in raw projected efficiency. Conversely, we are steering clear of **Wade Meckler** (39.79), as his profile falls below our 40.0 floor threshold today, and we must remain disciplined with our game caps.\n\nManagers should monitor the lineup status for **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**, though both are currently projected to lead off and provide solid efficiency ratings above 59.0. We are navigating a difficult stretch with **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining on the IL, placing additional pressure on our healthy starters to produce across the board. While **Jackson Merrill** (47.12) is active, exercise caution; his score is hampered by a difficult matchup against Boyd and an elite opposing catcher, making him a candidate for potential mid-game defensive substitution if the game situation dictates preserving cap efficiency.",
